[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-20071"] :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x-y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=5.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{4x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{4x}\\cdot {e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{4x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=5$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4\\cdot 0}}{4}+C) & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{4}+C) & =5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}+C & ={e}^{5} \\\\ C & =\\frac{4{e}^{5}-1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=5$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{4x}+4{e}^{5}-1}{4}).\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-355576/field-1/e8d9205bd708eb61e871039ac7460feaacd17607dc48f590232c13dd2390dc68" :answer/id #uuid "981c21a9-cb33-51cd-8856-ed2cd2b77e27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^2+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{e^{-2x}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355576/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a5c2a23-78b1-5d33-84b7-dd0a8ec0c257" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355576/field-1/e8d9205bd708eb61e871039ac7460feaacd17607dc48f590232c13dd2390dc68" :answer-field/choices ["q-355576/field-1/e8d9205bd708eb61e871039ac7460feaacd17607dc48f590232c13dd2390dc68"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355576" :question/id #uuid "c9a525de-458e-59f4-9fd7-b95961958051" :question/math-academy-id "q-355576" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-2x-y}$ given that  $\\,y(0)=2.$\n\n$y(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-2x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-2x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{0}+C) & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ C-\\frac{1}{2} & ={e}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{2{e}^{2}+1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-2x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=2$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{-{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{2}+1}{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-355576/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355576"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
